cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "mlflow-falsify: MLflow plugin for automatic PRML manifest hash tagging"
abstract: >-
  An MLflow Run Context Provider plugin that auto-discovers a PRML
  (Pre-Registered ML Manifest) v0.1 file in the working directory or any
  parent, computes its byte-equivalent canonical SHA-256, and tags every
  mlflow.start_run() with the manifest hash plus metric, comparator,
  threshold, and dataset id. Zero workflow change for MLflow users.
